Whollar Landing Page v7.html
Join the Waitlist (1).html
Whollar Admin Console.html

# Blog drafts not published yet
blogs

# Second, UNGUARDED copy of the member dashboard. dashboard.html has a
# front-end member check; this prototype has none, so deploying it publishes
# the signed-in surface at /whollar-member-dashboard-v8 to anyone with the URL.
whollar-member-dashboard-v8.html

# v10 prototype, same reason: pure-demo reference source for dashboard.html
# (its features were ported in), no login guard, must never deploy.
Consumerdashboard.html

# The v3 partner console. Superseded on 2026-08-15 by the v12 transplant that
# briefly ran at /provider, and both are now retired: the real console is
# partner/. Kept in the repo until sign-off so the change is easy to reverse by
# hand, and not published: it carries the full signed-in surface, and cleanUrls
# would otherwise serve a second, stale console at its own path.
provider-dashboard.legacy.html

# Reference prototypes being ported into real pages. Same reason again, and
# note docs/ itself IS deployed (the .md files are harmless), so an .html file
# left in docs/ would publish at /docs/prototype/<name>. The partner console
# v12 source has no login guard, no noindex, and a full signed-in surface.
docs/prototype

# The member-room network toggle design reference (a self-unpacking bundle,
# demo data, no guard). Its layout was ported into dashboard.html on
# 2026-08-14; cleanUrls would otherwise publish it at /socialmediatoggle.
socialmediatoggle.html

# The v17 checkup design reference (demo data, wire-up stubs, no analytics).
# Its behaviour was ported into bill-checkup.html on 2026-08-13; cleanUrls
# would otherwise publish this raw file at /overpaying.
overpaying.html

# The console's fixture states. Never deployed, which is what makes fixture
# mode genuinely unreachable in production: the file is not uploaded, so the
# request 404s regardless of query flags, hostname spoofing, or a bug in the
# gate the fixtures carry. scripts/build-console.mjs also skips demo/, so the
# fixtures are not in the bundle either and cannot arrive by an accidental
# import; this line covers the on-demand fetch that loads them. Fixture mode
# therefore works on localhost only, which is also where it matters, since
# dev-server.mjs proxies to the live Development backend and there is no local
# emulator.
partner/demo

# Self-contained page snapshots for sharing/offline use. They are copies of the
# live pages that do NOT receive fixes (their own README says edits don't flow
# either way) and they still POST to the live Catalyst backend. Shipping them
# put a third, stale copy of the checkup on the site.
standalone-pages

# Build inputs, not site assets: the mobile CSS overlays consumed by
# scripts/build-mobile-pages.mjs.
MobileVersion/overlays

# Working files no live page references (verified against every page,
# including the decoded bundle templates).
