saving-2.png

node_modules

# Source data for scripts/build-benchmarks.mjs. The site ships the generated
# js/whollar-benchmarks.js, not the 390 KB spreadsheet.
*.xlsx

# Pre-change copies kept only so a change is easy to reverse by hand. Not .html,
# so cleanUrls does not touch them, but they would still be served verbatim at
# their own path, and both carry the full signed-in join flow.
*.pre-form-reduction.bak

# Same reason, for the "Worth a read" pass. Named separately rather than folded
# into a single *.bak: a per-change name says which change a copy belongs to,
# and a copy nobody can date is a copy nobody deletes. All three carry a full
# signed-in dashboard.
*.pre-worth-a-read.bak

# Same reason again, for the Home layout pass. Carries the full signed-in
# dashboard, so it must never publish.
*.pre-layout-fix.bak

# The welcome-screen design reference (demo data, a Member/Partner preview
# toggle, no login guard). Split into the two real pages welcome-member.html
# and welcome-partner.html on 2026-08-15; cleanUrls would otherwise publish
# this raw file at /welcomewhollar, where the toggle would let anyone read
# both accounts' onboarding copy against fixture names.
welcomewhollar.html

# The v2 welcome-screen design reference. Same reason as welcomewhollar.html
# above: a Member/Partner preview toggle, fixture names ("Northline
# Internet"), no login guard and no noindex. Its layout was ported into
# welcome-member.html on 2026-08-17; cleanUrls would otherwise publish this
# raw file at /whollar-welcome-v2, where the toggle would let anyone read both
# accounts' onboarding copy.
whollar-welcome-v2.html

# Photograph originals for the cohort tiles. Build inputs, not site assets: the
# site ships the 300x130 and 600x260 crops under images/regions/, and these are
# full-resolution JPEGs (one is 2.9 MB) that no page references. Kept in the
# repo so a tile can be re-cropped from its source rather than re-sourced.
#
# Spelled with the capital C the directory actually has: this file is matched on
# the Linux builder, where campaignphotos and Campaignphotos are two different
# paths, so the lowercase spelling matched nothing and shipped every original,
# the 2.9 MB one included. macOS cannot show you that mistake.
Campaignphotos/

# The operator's guide to opening a cohort, kept in the repo as the printable
# companion to docs/COHORT_RUNBOOK.md. Same reason as docs/prototype above:
# docs/ itself IS deployed, so cleanUrls would publish the .html at
# /docs/console/cohort-launch-guide and serve the PDF verbatim beside it. It
# names internal steps and internal table columns and is written for staff.
docs/console/cohort-launch-guide.html
docs/console/cohort-launch-guide.pdf
